# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — never commit these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
serviceAccountKey.json
**/serviceAccountKey.json
*-service-account*.json

# google-services.json / GoogleService-Info.plist / firebase_options.dart are
# NOT secrets — Firebase client config (apiKey, appId, projectId, ...) is
# public by design; it ships inside every built app binary and Firebase's
# security model relies on Firestore/Storage Rules, not on hiding this.
# They're committed on purpose so `git pull` gives everyone the same
# correct kalinga-bc97f config instead of each dev generating their own via
# `flutterfire configure` (a step that's easy to point at the wrong/a new
# project by mistake — see README.md §3.3).

